sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Caller as CLI / REPL / Tests
    participant Main as main.rs
    participant Facade as session facade
    participant Repl as repl/eval module
    participant Deps as dependency-registration service
    participant Workers as worker subsystem
    participant Sched as scheduler.rs
    participant FE as frontend facade
    participant TC as typecheck facade
    participant BE as backend facade
    participant Cache as cache/object service

    Caller->>Main: run / repl / link
    Main->>Facade: CompilerSession::new + action dispatch

    alt REPL eval
        Facade->>Repl: parse command / eval source / reload hooks
        Repl->>FE: parse + expand + build
        Repl->>Deps: ensure dependency published+registered once
        Deps->>Sched: register / wait / unblock using one canonical protocol
        Repl->>TC: check_form / finalize
        Repl->>BE: compile/evaluate via canonical backend entrypoint
    else batch / link
        Facade->>Deps: register entry module once
        Deps->>Sched: enqueue module work
        Sched->>Workers: priority or object work item
        Workers->>FE: parse/extract/build through facade only
        Workers->>Deps: resolve discovered deps through same canonical service
        Workers->>TC: check/check_form only
        Workers->>BE: JIT or object compile through canonical backend entrypoint
        Workers->>Cache: cache-hit load / object write through one cache service
        Workers->>Sched: notify typecheck / codegen completion
    end

    Facade-->>Caller: values / diagnostics / link result

    Note right of Facade: Session core stays thin after the split.
    Note over Repl,Deps: REPL and dependency registration share one protocol.
    Note right of Workers: Priority and nice workers live in one subsystem.
    Note over FE,BE: Integration consumes narrow child crate facades.
    Note over Caller,Facade: The public surface is small and stable.
